        <p>Warrington is at the present time suffering !rota something like an epidemic of deaths amongst ita most prominent citizens. The tatrst loss is through the tient!) of Mr. J. /I. Fleming, member of 910 Town Council and • magiatrate. Mr. Fleming bad not been so long resident in Warrington a, the late Dr. Smith or NI, Timms. Morrin,but during the net twelve or Merin years he took a fairly conspicu- ous part in much of the public luminarss of the town. Both in imperial and municipal politics he had enlightened opinions and could always be re- lied upon to support Greasily, of a progremise character.</p>
