        <head>DR. WEIR'S POROUS PLASTER</head>
        <p>DR. WEIR'S POROUS PLASTER</p>
        <p>WAHRINOTON V. LEIOH.</p>
        <p>A NAM) (JANE. After a series of meritorious victories, and two of them away from home. the Warrington team awaited the visit of Leigh On Saturday with confi- dente of their ability to annex ancit.l.r couple of innate. A gate numbering about 7,0.10 lined the en- clo.ure, arid so both teams turned out their full strength there was rev...mole anticipation of • good game. It proved rather too good lor the homemers, who got. shaking which should teat i them.! whole/tome Meson. The weather *foul was all that 1 could be desired troth a spectator • point at view, but it was rather sultry for the bonne teams. As a ' l sort of reward for their prowess the lionmeters turned out m new jerseys, and preeerneel an appear- lance 111.1C11 smarter than ordinary. The Lmghites were much the heavier. No wind bothered the I players so that the choice of positions Tra, not of great importance. Coop defended the railway goal In the Arm ball. Mr. C. Williams, of Salford, was the referee rut the players ware an follow.: W•IMIN(M.: B meow, NB back; Barber, Cruel, I Isherwood arid Boon. threequartere ; Bate and lligginbottom, holt hack., Taylor. Dakiii, llatratt, Sin, ',a.m.., Schott., 'Thornton and Naylor for- wards. • Limit l Gov, lull bath; Andercon, ' idhlgson, thr.req oarter. ; Slolyneux and Uunlismo, halt-had.; I'. Taylor. R. Taylor, Boardman, Clieethato, rrauce, litri.t on, Shaw, and</p>
